  <bioghist id="aspace_9b07c9c26ad78ff0de16fe2d43589d70">
    <head>Biography/History</head>
<p>Born in 1925, Ebherhard Brüning was a retired professor of American Studies at Leipzig University, Germany. He worked as the literary agent of various authors, including Albert Maltz, one of the Hollywood Ten, from the early 1950s until Maltz's death in 1985. In addition, he translated some of Maltz's novels, short stories and plays into German.</p>  </bioghist>
  <scopecontent id="aspace_f985e268fb11c50512fc7edd6a70bb40">
    <head>Scope and Content</head>
<p>This collection consists of materials related to the career of literary agent Eberhard Brüning. Included are correspondence, manuscripts, newspaper clippings, photographs, audio recordings and playbills,relating tp various authors, particularly Albert Maltz, one of the Hollywood Ten.</p>  </scopecontent>
